      "id": "task-computation",
      "finding": "No task-computation substitution found in these 12 adapters: model construction/weights, inputs, dtype, work amount and required outputs agree with source; recorded independent checks all pass. Qwen and ResNet reference-output errors are zero; DDP serial-global-batch checks cover full gradients and parameters for two consecutive updates within the original tolerance.",
      "limits": "Finite declared inputs only. Numerical fidelity does not prove identical timing, allocator lifetime, unseen inputs, or convergence."
    },
    {
      "id": "qwen-metric-window",
      "finding": "Both throughput adapters divide all 32 generated tokens by framework outer elapsed_ms, whereas original infer() reports its internal generation interval. TTFT adapters retain the explicit first-token-ready synchronization boundary.",
      "evidence": "Both saved throughput baselines expose outer and internal timestamps in each same sample; see timing below.",
      "effect": "Observed baseline denominator difference is small; it does not by itself invalidate the fixed-adapter paired result. Candidate overhead and direct original-entry speedup are not measured by this audit."
    },
    {
      "id": "resnet-instrumentation",
      "finding": "Final latency and memory adapters reset/read allocator statistics inside run(); the source resets before starting its timer and reads after stopping. The adapters also add synchronization/phase wrappers to the framework's outer timing. Development latency adapter leaves the extra allocator operations outside run().",
      "effect": "The timing boundaries are not identical. Overhead magnitude has not been isolated here."
    },
    {
      "id": "resnet-persistent-assets",
      "finding": "Final latency adapter retains only selected pixels, not the full GPU images fixture retained by the source. Both memory adapters retain images and pixels. Model outputs match the source.",
      "effect": "Final latency adapter memory metrics must not be treated as an exact reproduction of the source's allocator residency; this finding is not present in the reported final memory-goal adapter."
    },
    {
      "id": "ddp-gradient-clearing",
      "finding": "Final ddp-step and development ddp-communication call zero_grad(set_to_none=True) in reset() as well as in run(). The source clears gradients in accumulate() inside timed step(), with reset() restoring weights only. Development ddp-step and final ddp-communication retain the source location.",
      "effect": "Gradient release work can move outside timing despite equivalent numerical updates. Its performance effect has not been isolated. The development DDP-step positive result uses the adapter retaining source placement."
    },
    {
      "id": "communication-reasoning",
      "finding": "The final DDP communication candidate describes calibration as a pure-transfer floor and infers that re-bucketing/coalescing is ruled out. Its actual tool response had already displayed the caveat that calibration is not a model schedule reproduction or lower bound.",
      "evidence": "stage2-autonomy-final-21897c1/ddp-communication/trials/trial-b5a0778f8a/proposal.json and actual_tool_delivery below.",
      "effect": "This is an evidenced interpretation problem, not proof that additional collector fields are needed. Delivery does not establish correct comprehension."
    }
